{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":484754,"name":"Eric Han","username":"Eric_Han","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/eb8c5e/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T00:21:53.496Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484754-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484754-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484754-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484754-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery message to Grok Bot fails with an error that it cannot generate a reply\u003cbr\u003e\n(Bot failed to respond / Something went wrong while generating the reply).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis happens on simple messages such as “hello”, not only tool/computer-use tasks.\u003cbr\u003e\nIt affects existing conversations and a newly created bot as well.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Agent Computer / VM screen is still visible.\u003cbr\u003e\nI can see the desktop (and the box looks reachable), but the bot never generates a reply.\u003cbr\u003e\nSo this does not look like a local app crash or a “can’t reach computer” issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484754-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484754-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen an existing bot (or create a new one).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSend a short message with no tools/connectors/memory, e.g. “hello”.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe error appears within a few seconds.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Agent Computer — the VM screen is still visible.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484754-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484754-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe bot should generate a reply. A simple “hello” should work even if computer-use is not needed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484754-what-i-already-tried-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484754-what-i-already-tried-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat I already tried\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit and reopen Grok Bot (not just closing the window)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSent a short test message in a new chat\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreated a new bot — same failure\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAgent Computer screen remains visible\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI have not repeatedly reset the computer, to avoid putting the box into a partial state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484754-additional-context-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484754-additional-context-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional context\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis matches previous reports where the account’s shared cloud computer was stuck on the generation side while the desktop view still loaded. All bots share one computer, which would explain why a new bot fails the same way.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease recover/rebuild the Agent Computer on the account side if needed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484754-environment-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484754-environment-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eEnvironment\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProduct: Grok Bot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOS: [macOS / Windows / Android / iOS]\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot version: [e.g. 0.43.0]\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAccount email: [your Cursor account email]\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConversation ID (if available): 